PanVK (Mesa 26.2.6, MIT; Mesa's notices are kept as they are): what closed each batch, for the DRM shim's statistics.

Every cmd_close_batch caller names why (end of rendering, barrier, before a dispatch, the dispatch, begin rendering, job
limit, end of the command buffer, event, query); the shim (tools/ios27/mesa-ios/starbite-drm, which defines the counters)
prints "drm[pid] vk batches N: ..." every 10 s with STARBITE_DRM_STATS=1. Counters only: nothing else changes.
Recorded on 17 November 2026 from the local tree (s9-night-ui) the 14 November PanVK was built from, with one correction:
there, two `if` statements of panvk_vX_cmd_query.c without braces got the counter's assignment as their whole body, so
cmd_close_batch ran unconditionally after them; here they close only where Mesa closes.

--- a/src/panfrost/vulkan/jm/panvk_vX_cmd_buffer.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/vulkan/jm/panvk_vX_cmd_buffer.c
@@ -88,10 +88,20 @@
 }
 #endif
 
